+- **Action:** Retitled to canonical capitalization ("Key facts"/"Key dates"/"Application due date") and forced to `h4`. A qualifying paragraph supplies the editable title and is removed from the body. Keep the paragraph in the body when it contains a link, nested bookmark or other non-text content. Keep the remaining body and links. Keep the supplied deadline title rather than renaming it or synthesizing another box. Preserve date text and links to ordinary Key dates content. New imports and authorized re-imports share this behavior; no saved-record migration or template-date gate. At rendering, named Application due date callouts use the same first-section portrait sidebar as legacy Key dates; their simple date/link body does not receive the legacy colon formatting. Both source boxes, if supplied, remain in source order with no selection or deletion. Plain headings/prose are not floating callouts.
 - **Source:** `content_processing.py::get_subsections_from_sections` (`key_callout_titles`)
